nstellium SE Ordinary Shares (France) (CSTM). This chart runs from Jun 14, 2017 to Oct 19, 2017.","setup":"The stock rose about 81% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 3 weeks, peaking at $10.95 and pulling back 13% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Aug 31, 2017 it closed at $11.30, its first close above the base high of $10.95. Volume that day was 2.1M shares, 3.07x the prior 10-day average of 680K. It didn't hold. By Sep 12, 2017 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $10.75.","lesson":"This is an example of a failed breakout where everything looked right, volume included, and the stock fell back anyway. It happens. This is why traders cut losses fast instead of hoping."}}